"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"callout-title\",\"className\":\"text-rem20px font-bold self-center leading-rem22px bp1100:leading-rem24px text-gray-900\",\"children\":\"Care at Cleveland Clinic\"}]]}]}],\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"callout-links\",\"className\":\"justify-start pb-rem24px space-y-rem24px\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"callout-link-0\",{\"data-identity\":\"callout-detailed-link\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"callout-link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/services/primary-care\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 font-medium underline underline-offset-[5px] dec"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"oration-1 hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":\"Find a Primary Care Provider\"}],null]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"callout-link-1\",{\"data-identity\":\"callout-detailed-link\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"callout-link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/services/primary-care#call-to-action-panel\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 font-medium underline underline-offset-[5px] decoration-1 hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":\"Schedule an Appointment\"}],null]}]]}]]}]}]\n6b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"a827639000a5\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"With research ongoing, many healthcare providers still recommend the RICE method, but they’re more specific now about how to apply it. In many cases, the RICE method may still be appropriate for immediate relief after an injury, but not for long-term recovery. Sometimes, reducing pain, swelling or bleeding is the most immediate medical priority. Other times, a different protocol might work better.\"]}]\n6c:[\"$\",\"div\",\"a827639000a5_mobile_ad\",{\"data-identity\":\"billboard-ad\",\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden print:hidden max-w-[400px] min-w-[300px] m-auto items-center justify-center bg-gray-300 pt-rem16px pb-[3.125rem] my-rem32px  \",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-[300px] mx-auto\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 uppercase text-rem10px leading-rem16px mx-auto w-fit\",\"children\":\"Advertisement\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden flex-col items-center justify-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"ad-slot\",\"id\":\"billboard5_300x250_mobile\",\"className\":\"ad-reset w-[300px] !min-h-[250px] flex bg-gray-300\"}],null]}]]}]}]\n6d:[\"$\",\"h3\",\"7cfb80fa5e9a\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem30px text-rem25px bp600:text-rem32px bp600:leading-rem38px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"What are the alternatives to the RICE method for treating an injury?\"]}]\n6e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"103608828cbd\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"In recent years, healthcare providers have suggested some new, alternative protocols for treating soft tissue injuries at home: MEAT, and PEACE \u0026 LOVE. They recommend these for long-term recovery after the acute phase of your injury (the first 72 hours). You may still use the RICE method in the acute phase.\"]}]\n6f:[\"$\",\"h4\",\"9fecda217341\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem24px text-rem20px bp600:text-rem25px bp600:leading-rem30px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-bold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"MEAT injury method\"]}]\n70:[\"$\",\"p\",\"2c8f897e6886\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"MEAT stands for:\"]}]\n71:[\"$\",\"ul\",\"d4f74c13f5b9-parent\",{\"data-identity\":\"unordered-list\",\"className\":\"my-rem16px mx-0 pl-[1.25rem] list-disc marker:text-brandBlue-500 print:marker:text-black marker:pl-rem24px print:my-rem8px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal  \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"d4f74c13f5b9\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"2fca528ac05b0\",{\"children\":[\"Movement\"]}],\". Gentle movement from time to time encourages blood flow to your injured tissues to promote healing. Let"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1," pain be your guide as to how much movement is too much, too soon.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"024b8d9ee8c2\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"cb5fda2cf03e0\",{\"children\":[\"Exercise\"]}],\". As you begin to heal, you may begin to introduce specific, controlled exercises to help rehabilitate your injured part. A \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"cb5fda2cf03e2\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/articles/24625-physical-therapist\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"physical therapist\"]}],\" can show you what to do, and how.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"9270163f8e95\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"0078a00d6eaa0\",{\"children\":[\"Analgesia\"]}],\". \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"0078a00d6eaa2\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/drugs/21483-analgesics\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"Analgesics\"]}],\" are pain relievers. You may need to continue to use \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"0078a00d6eaa4\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/12058-pain-relievers\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"pain relievers\"]}],\" during your recovery to allow for enough healthy movement. Follow your healthcare provider’s advice.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"26e5bb27d47a\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"a9ab95c3bada0\",{\"children\":[\"Therapy\"]}],\". Therapy encompasses the many long-term treatments you may need to fully recover from an injury. Your provider might recommend orthotics, bodywork or other modalities.\"]}]]}]\n72:[\"$\",\"h4\",\"b78adef68b8c\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem24px text-rem20px bp600:text-rem25px bp600:leading-rem30px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-bold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"PEACE \u0026 LOVE injury method\"]}]\n73:[\"$\",\"p\",\"a9adbe3dabea\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"PEACE \u0026 LOVE stands for:\"]}]\n74:[\"$\",\"ul\",\"0fd5b41dba9f-parent\",{\"data-identity\":\"unordered-list\",\"className\":\"my-rem16px mx-0 pl-[1.25rem] list-disc marker:text-brandBlue-500 print:marker:text-black marker:pl-rem24px print:my-rem8px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal  \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"0fd5b41dba9f\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"893179c26c270\",{\"children\":[\"Protection\"]}],\". To protect the injury during healing, you might need to wear a cast, brace or splint.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"d740648142a0\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"60f75d5eba090\",{\"children\":[\"Elevation\"]}],\". While resting your injury, keep it elevated to reduce blood flow and swelling.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"d1690950a839\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem1"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"50c3cdba374b0\",{\"children\":[\"Avoid anti-inflammatories\"]}],\". Providers now recommend pain relievers that don’t suppress inflammation after the first few days of recovery. That means \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"50c3cdba374b2\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/drugs/18829-acetaminophen-capsules-or-tablets\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"acetaminophen\"]}],\" instead of \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"50c3cdba374b4\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/11086-non-steroidal-anti-inflammatory-medicines-nsaids\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"NSAIDs\"]}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"8eda9992a3f6\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"625bad06fc140\",{\"children\":[\"Compression\"]}],\". A compression bandage on your injury can reduce swelling and bleeding.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"e633123a3c02\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"ea86885ca1230\",{\"children\":[\"Education\"]}],\". This is to remind healthcare providers to educate you about your role in your own recovery. Specifically, they should encourage you to play an active rather than passive role.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"0c61e9752192\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"382729e45d5f0\",{\"children\":[\"Load\"]}],\". Loading means gradually returning some mechanical load (weight or stress) to your injured part. Your provider might refer you to a physical therapist to guide this process.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"6c02f221cf1a\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"9ab0feabbabd0\",{\"children\":[\"Optimism\"]}],\". Research has found that a positive approach to recovery can affect your prognosis (outlook). Believe in your own capacity to heal, and don’t neglect your mental health during recovery.\"]}],\"$L7e\",\"$L7f\"]}]\n77:[\"$\",\"span\",\"125dd09642111\",{\"className\":\"break-words\",\"children\":[[\"Management of acute soft tissue injury using Protection Rest Ice Compression and Elevation: Recommendations from the Association of Chartered Physiotherapists in Sports Medicine (ACPSM)\"],[\" \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":[\"(\",\"https://www.physiosinsport.org/media/wysiwyg/ACPSM_Physio_Price_A4.pdf\",\")\"]}]]]}]\n78:[\"$\",\"li\",\"3d72c0b38727\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem15px leading-rem19px marker:text-rem19px print:text-rem13px print:leading-rem16px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Scialoia, D., Swartzendruber, A. \",[\"$\",\"span\",\"6efff54c6af31\",{\"className\":\"break-words\",\"children\":[[\"The R.I.C.E Protocol is a MYTH: A Review and Recommendations\"],[\" \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":[\"(\",\"https://thesportjournal.org/article/the-r-i-c-e-protocol-is-a-myth-a-review-and-recommendations/\",\")\"]}]]]}],\". \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"6efff54c6af33\",{\"children\":[\"The Sport Journal\"]}],\". 2020 Nov 12;4. Accessed 1/22/2025.\"]}]\n79:[\"$\",\"li\",\"1eb898273885\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem15px leading-rem19px marker:text-rem19px print:text-rem13px print:leading-rem16px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"van den Bekerom MP, Struijs PA, Blankevoort L, Welling L, at al. \",[\"$\",\"span\",\"a404de454bad1\",{\"className\":\"break-words\",\"children\":[[\"What is the evidence for rest, ice, compression, and elevation therapy in the"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1," treatment of ankle sprains in adults?\"],